A||||22||Nashco||Who has pulled the most G's?||||1||
Z||000000||Nashco||11-12-2001||08:01 PM||||I got into an argument with a guy at work today about how the Fiero handles, and I was wondering who has pulled the most Gs?!?<P>I told him I hope to have my car pulling a G before I graduate, and I honestly do plan on it.  He tells me there's no way, that I'm looking at spending about two grand to get it happening, if at all.<P>I'm sure not many people have access to accelerometers, but since we have a lot of autocrossers someone has to know.  I thought that 1.1 and 1.2 G would be standard for the highest class Fieros.<P>So, who can help me out?  Anybody at least have an idea of what the highest they've heard was?<P>Thanks <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||85ZainoGT||11-12-2001||08:22 PM||||thats a lot of G's man, sure is possible though, but will be a good amount of $$$. I know the new z06's are pulling 1.1?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 Gold GT 2.8L<BR>All the options :)<BR>  pics are coming :)||||reg||6
Z||000002||Spektrum-87GT||11-12-2001||08:23 PM||||i pulled about 4 in my turn the other day  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||11-12-2001||08:33 PM||||I don't think that the centrifugal force of spinning out counts though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||AkursedX||11-12-2001||09:23 PM||||I know someone on this board has pulled 1.16G's on DOT legal tires  (1Fst2m6??)<P>I believe my car is up around 1G (88 KYB's, POLY, lowering springs, 17inch rims and big sticky tires  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> )  But I would like to get it tested.<P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Master_Sushi||11-12-2001||09:55 PM||||Has anyone had this happen before? My 88 coupe really loved corners. It was mostly a stock setup, and I had 16 inch Kumho tires.<P>If I would push it in a twisty I could get windshield washer fluid to squirt out of the nozzles and all over the windshield. I checked and didn’t have a lose hose or anything either. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>Whenever I was driving with somebody, this would allways make them laugh <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.||||reg||5
Z||000006||Standard||11-12-2001||09:59 PM||||Yeah, it was Trav (1fst2m6) who had his gold notchback above 1g.  With a real driver  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Some good modern rubber should get a stock Fiero around .9g... lowered, poly, bigger wheels, good alignment and a good driver should get 1g+ no problem.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Eric||11-12-2001||11:41 PM||||It's been a long time, but I think I recorded .94 gs with my 88GT stock except for A509s on the original wheels.||||reg||1
Z||000008||87FieroGTx||11-12-2001||11:51 PM|||| About a year ago I had an 87 Fiero GT (Hence my name) with Koni's, lowered 1 1/2", full polly and Pzero's it would pull 1.1g easy! I spent around $1,600 but you could do it for way less $$$ if you don't use Koni's(There one of the best but expensive) Then my garage burnt down and it was lost <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P> My new 85's suspension is mostly stock but still out handles my 95 Trans Am. I'm building more of a drag car this time.<P>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT ~ auto 3.2 200hp 220tq ~ 75+ shot NOS ~ 0-60 4.9 13.5 1/4||||reg||1
Z||000009||Formula88||11-12-2001||11:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Master_Sushi:<BR><B>If I would push it in a twisty I could get windshield washer fluid to squirt out of the nozzles and all over the windshield. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So THAT's where it's coming from!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Yup, same thing happens in my Formula when I get into the twisties.  And that was with my worn out OEM suspension.  I can't wait to see how much washer fluid I can slosh out with my new KYB's!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||L.I. Fieros||11-13-2001||12:03 AM||||When my 86SE was lowered I pulled 1.01 G's as measured using a G-Tech.  Hitting 0.92 was easy, getting up around 0.98 - 1.0 was not so easy.  Balance is everything!  This was on regular tires (nothing special) with urethane bushings everywhere, bigger front sway bar, addition of a rear bar, new KYB's, lowering springs, bump steer modified rear, and a good alignment.  The "usual" Fiero mods.  Oh, and my car would have easily been beaten by my friends (even lower) 86.  The over-all ride and "daily driveability" did suffer though (from the lowering springs), which is why they have since been passed along.  Oh, and if memory serves me correctly it was all slightly less than $1K.<P>See ya,<BR>Dave||||reg||6
Z||000011||artherd||11-13-2001||05:22 AM||||Heck, throw a set of 17s and decent rubber on there, add new shocks, lowering springs and poly, and you're easially over 1G in any Fiero....<P>These cars are go-karts man.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000012||rogergarrison||11-13-2001||07:24 AM||||does doing 1,000 mph turns in an F4 Phantom count? If so I guess I win..... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||California Kid||11-13-2001||10:00 AM||||My '88 will pull 1.17g, it's lowered 1.5, urethane, koni's, Comp T/A's.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_7.jpg"> ||||reg||1
