Z||000018||3.8T Fiero GT||11-13-2001||08:31 PM||||i have a gtech and am soooooooo waiting to try it this spring on the car, i will le ty aguys know!<P>i am SO wanting to know how a done fiero handles...cause all my civic friends say it wont, i am like "kiss my ass" <P>they dunno **** !<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cache.ucr.edu/~currie/turbo-t.jpg">  <BR><B>"A 3.8T makes and excellent "RICE" cooker"</B>||||reg||1
Z||000019||Nashco||11-14-2001||02:08 AM||||This is exactly the boost I needed guys, you all rule!  About six hours after I posted that I got that, "I don't care what he thinks anyway!" feeling.  Now I'm all psyched <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Along with my new motor mounts, 17s, front suspension (konis, springs, poly, balljoints), and the next on the list being rear poly and coilovers....I'm thinking I should be in the market for a Gtech too <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Sweet!  I can't wait to feel a full G!  I'm thinking of a custom plate/name for the car...G spot <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  That car may as well be my G spot..cause it makes me feel gooood <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>Oh, by the way....does anybody already have that name for their Fiero? I just thought of that...I am sure somebody does, if not, I thought of it first, don't steal it!!! LOL<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000020||ChopTop||11-14-2001||09:29 AM||||You may want to pick up the December issue of Sport Compact Car.  It's featuring G-Games, and has several cars fighting for handling supremacy.  <BR>10-Subaru WRX---.874g<BR>9-Acura Type R--.913g<BR>8-Honda del Sol-.926g<BR>7-Classic VW Beetle-.937g<BR>6-Toyota Supra---.948g<BR>5-Ford Escourt---.956g<BR>4-Porsche 914-6--.985g<BR>3-Toyota Supra---1.009g<BR>2-Classic VW Bettle-1.011g<BR>1-Mazda RX7------1.035g||||reg||1
Z||000021||Nashco||11-14-2001||11:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ChopTop:<BR><B>You may want to pick up the December issue of Sport Compact Car.  It's featuring G-Games, and has several cars fighting for handling supremacy.  <BR>10-Subaru WRX---.874g<BR>9-Acura Type R--.913g<BR>8-Honda del Sol-.926g<BR>7-Classic VW Beetle-.937g<BR>6-Toyota Supra---.948g<BR>5-Ford Escourt---.956g<BR>4-Porsche 914-6--.985g<BR>3-Toyota Supra---1.009g<BR>2-Classic VW Bettle-1.011g<BR>1-Mazda RX7------1.035g</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This article is actually what sparked the entire issue.  I was surprised that's all that these cars pulled, as I know the Fieros pull that easily.  I mentioned that a well modded Fiero should have been in there.  They had a three rotor RX7, why not a V8 or turbo Fiero?  I know we can pull more Gs, and a V8 fiero would be wicked fast.  My coworkers were giving me the  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> reaction.<P>What do you guys think?  I know we're a little biased, but I honestly believe a Fiero with as much money tied up as that RX7 did would put up a hell of a fight.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000022||Slammed Fiero||11-14-2001||11:01 AM||||Steady State G's are not the greatest measure of a cars ability to handle. How often do you drive in a 300ft circle?<P>you could throw a set of Koni's and stiff springs on a lebaron and generate some impressive numbers.<P>Funny sport compact car left off an 84 Corvette which broke 1G back in the day (z51 package) with old crappy Goodyears.<P>As for the Civics...A prepped Civic will handle better than any Fiero here, 88 or not, modded to hell and back. Check your local autocross.<P>Light weight , better inital design and platform give new cars a huge advantage over us.<P>JM <P>On a GTEC with Street pirelli's I got 1.14 G's on a Vericom. I have since swapped to coilovers upfront. To generate this kind of Number the car rides like a tank.<p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 11-14-2001).]||||reg||1
